            "vuln_file": "net/core/dev.c",
            "stmt_text": "if (!shinfo->gso_size) {",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This is the entry point of qdisc_pkt_len_segs_init() function. The vulnerability exists because this function handles GSO packet initialization but only pulls TCP headers for TCP GSO types (lines 4134-4135 mentioned in rationale) while lacking equivalent header-pulling validation for other GSO types. When shinfo->gso_size is non-zero (indicating GSO packet), the function fails to ensure all GSO packet headers are pulled into the linear skb->head buffer, allowing downstream code to perform direct copies on skb->data that may access uninitialized or non-linear memory regions."
          }
        ]
      }
